{"id": "EUVD-2026-86207", "enisaUuid": "96d52375-0262-3575-8760-bd48fc2e1281", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nPCI: mediatek: Protect root bus removal with rescan lock\n\nHold the pci_rescan_remove_lock lock while stopping and removing a root bus\nto avoid racing with concurrent rescan or hotplug operations triggered via\nsysfs.  Such races may lead to use-after-free issues or system crashes.\n\n[bhelgaas: commit log]", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:02:56", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:57:50", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d54417acb22d9e8bc404a8598330bc9729ee7146", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5dd379acfa38c516e904bcfa693502cd585a0bba", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8d910649725955435c6a807944108bca0570712d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31e33dcc896527b3ad790fdc6aa6b8d2995c078b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c57b971765f835138fa2fce3f2a171b004cbb114", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a568939487dcbc1a3e341208585e224be897e25e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a29812a55da8d0dbeb071b26ac428c338e3fc389"], "aliases": ["GHSA-49r5-mv79-qprq", "CVE-2026-93819"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11a914cf-e5cd-3097-aaf9-143243711ade", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.222"}, {"id": "2ca62d4f-c784-379d-8f09-f4bee8bca4ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.20"}, {"id": "6a818846-6d6e-3b6a-85e3-7fd40a610f5a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "6e5c9d38-c7a9-3e5b-91b4-3490214a3359", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "76d97945-43ca-3191-a166-edf918be425c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "031337ace2d1c22a447da6390716fe92592cdd6e <31e33dcc896527b3ad790fdc6aa6b8d29